  "division": {
    "number": 1,
    "heading": "Lawyers’ Charges, Retainer Agreements and Right of Review"
  },
  "subdivision": {
    "number": 2,
    "heading": "Retainer Agreements"
  },
  "operative_text": {
    "controlling": "10.6(1)  In a retainer agreement or otherwise, a provision is void if\nthe provision\n(a) purports to relieve a lawyer from liability for negligence\nor any other liability to which the lawyer might be subject\nas a lawyer, or\n(b) purports to provide that an action, application or\nproceeding cannot be abandoned, discontinued or settled\nwithout a lawyer’s consent.\n(2)  Despite any agreement to the contrary, a client may change the\nclient’s lawyer or act on the client’s own behalf before a retainer\nagreement ends.",
    "controlling_carrier": "OFFICIAL",
    "sha256": "d1c548ce95a0d1c9f7e4582171b3ea0e8eeaa5f1e08fccd055afa155dcb017f5"
  },
